  "source": "canonical Group Anagrams concept; description, examples, and tests re-authored",
  "description": "Given a list of words, group the words that are anagrams of each other: they contain exactly the same characters with the same counts. Return the groups as a list of lists, with the words inside each group in alphabetical order and the groups themselves ordered by their first word.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= len(words) <= 2000",
    "each word is 1 to 40 lowercase letters"
  ],
  "parameters": ["words"],
  "functionName": "group_anagrams",
  "starterCode": "def group_anagrams(words):\n    # Return the anagram groups as a list of lists, sorted inside and outside.\n    ...\n",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": { "words": ["spot", "tops", "opts", "loop", "pool", "cat"] },
      "output": [["cat"], ["loop", "pool"], ["opts", "spot", "tops"]],
      "explanation": "spot, tops and opts use the same letters, as do loop and pool"
    },
    {
      "input": { "words": ["one"] },
      "output": [["one"]],
      "explanation": "a single word forms a group on its own"
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Two words are anagrams exactly when sorting their letters produces the same sequence.",
    "A dictionary can map that sorted-letter signature to the list of words sharing it.",
    "Build a signature for each word (its letters sorted), collect words under their key, then sort each group and sort the groups themselves."
  ],
  "solution": "Sort the letters of each word to get a signature and use it as a dictionary key mapping to a group of words. Afterwards sort the words inside every group and sort the groups by their first word for a deterministic answer. Building the groups is O(n k log k) for n words of length k.",
  "solutionCode": "def group_anagrams(words):\n    groups = {}\n    for word in words:\n        key = ''.join(sorted(word))\n        groups.setdefault(key, []).append(word)\n    result = [sorted(group) for group in groups.values()]\n    result.sort()\n    return result\n",
  "bruteForceCode": "def group_anagrams(words):\n    remaining = []\n    for word in words:\n        placed = False\n        for group in remaining:\n            if sorted(word) == sorted(group[0]):\n                group.append(word)\n                placed = True\n                break\n        if not placed:\n            remaining.append([word])\n    return sorted(sorted(group) for group in remaining)\n",
  "failureHint": "hidden tests include single-word lists, repeated words, and a large list where most words share letters",
  "expectedComplexity": { "time": "O(n k log k)", "space": "O(n k)" },
